{
  "case": "release notes from merged PRs",
  "variant": "without",
  "trial": 2,
  "run": {
    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 release notes to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. The version comes from `VERSION` and the date (2026-10-20) from `RELEASE_DATE`.\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * BREAKING: Remove deprecated --legacy flag from sync (ACME-421)\n  * CSV exporter for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **Format:** I followed the existing entries: short lines with the ticket ID at the end, no authors.\n- **Breaking change:** ACME-421 has a `!` in `merged_prs.txt`, which marks it as breaking, so I listed it first with a \"BREAKING:\" label.\n\n**Decision for you:** removing a flag is a breaking change, but `VERSION` is set to 2.4.0, a minor release. If you follow semantic versioning, this should probably be 3.0.0. I left the version as it is; tell me if you want it bumped and I'll update `VERSION` and the notes.",
